==Battleground==
*Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*20 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>, delay 16.67~20 seconds<sup>500f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Cerberus Kids]] spawn after 16.67 seconds<sup>500f</sup>, delay 16.67~23.33 seconds<sup>500f~700f</sup>.
*8 [[Star Peng]]s spawn after 26.67 seconds<sup>800f</sup>, delay 20~26.67 seconds<sup>600f~800f</sup>.
*2 [[Project A]]s spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 66.67~70 seconds<sup>2,000f~2,100f</sup>.
*4 [[General GreGory|General GreGories]] spawn after 46.67 seconds<sup>1,400f</sup>, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
*20 [[Sinner Snache]]s spawn after 66.67 seconds<sup>2,000f</sup>, delay 6~8 seconds<sup>180f~240f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage acts as a treasure/progress check for [[Cats of the Cosmos]], as it almost requires all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures|anti-starred alien treasures]]. Without them, the Star Pengs will have up to '''5 million''' health each.

Most common anti-alien units (notably [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer]] and [[Psychocat (Rare Cat)|Corrupted Psychocat]]) will help greatly with this stage. [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]] and [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut]] will also work well, since they can take advantage of the Project As' warp.

